cess contact form submissions\\\\n  - AuthHandler: Manage login/logout flows\\\\n  - ContentHandler: CRUD operations for news/events\\\\n  - PageDataHandler: Serve dynamic content for private pages\\\\n\\\\n### 4. Data Storage\\\\n- **DynamoDB Tables**:\\\\n  - Users: Store additional user profile data\\\\n  - NewsEvents: Store news and events with timestamps\\\\n  - Dues: Store dues information per resident\\\\n  - Meetings: Store annual meeting information\\\\n  - ContactSubmissions: Log contact form entries\\\\n- **S3 Content Bucket**: Store uploaded images/documents for news/events\\\\n\\\\n### 5. Communication\\\\n- **SES (Simple Email Service)**: Send emails from contact form and notifications\\\\n\\\\n### 6. Content Management\\\\n- **S3 Admin Bucket**: Store simple JSON/Markdown files for content\\\\n- **Lambda Admin Functions**: Provide simple API for updating content\\\\n- **Pre-signed URLs**: Allow secure file uploads without AWS credentials\\\\n\\\\n## Data Flow Examples\\\\n\\\\n### Public Page Access\\\\n1. User visits website → CloudFront → S3 static files\\\\n2. Static pages load with JavaScript that can fetch public data if needed\\\\n\\\\n### Resident Login & Private Access\\\\n1. User enters credentials → API Gateway → Lambda AuthHandler → Cognito\\\\n2. Cognito returns JWT tokens\\\\n3. Frontend stores tokens and includes in subsequent requests\\\\n4. Private page requests → API Gateway → Lambda Authorizer validates token → Lambda PageDataHandler → DynamoDB → Return data\\\\n\\\\n### Contact Form Submission\\\\n1. User fills form → API Gateway → Lambda ContactFormHandler\\\\n2. Lambda validates input → Stores in DynamoDB → Sends email via SES\\\\n3. Returns success/failure to user\\\\n\\\\n### News & Events Management (Non-technical User)\\\\n1. Admin logs in with special Cognito group permissions\\\\n2. Simple web interface allows:\\\\n   - Creating/editing posts via forms\\\\n   - Uploading images to S3 via pre-signed URLs\\\\n   - Publishing/unpublishing content\\\\n3. Changes stored in DynamoDB and immediately reflected on website\\\\n\\\\n## Security Considerations\\\\n- All data in transit encrypted via HTTPS (CloudFront)\\\\n- API Gateway throttling to prevent abuse\\\\n- Cognito handles password policies and MFA options\\\\n- Lambda functions use least-privilege IAM roles\\\\n- S3 buckets configured with proper access policies\\\\n- CORS properly configured for API endpoints\\\\n\\\\n## Scalability & Cost Benefits\\\\n- Serverless architecture scales automatically\\\\n- Pay only for actual usage (requests, storage, compute time)\\\\n- No server maintenance required\\\\n- CloudFront caching reduces backend load\\\\n- DynamoDB on-demand pricing ideal for variable traffic\\\\n\\\\n## Implementation Approach\\\\n1. Set up core infrastructure (S3, CloudFront, Route 53)\\\\n2. Implement authentication (Cognito, authorizer)\\\\n3. Build API endpoints and Lambda functions\\\\n4. Create DynamoDB tables and data models\\\\n5. Develop frontend with authentication flow\\\\n6. Implement CMS functionality for news/events\\\\n7. Configure SES and contact form\\\\n8. Testing and deployment\\\\n\\\\nThis architecture provides a robust, scalable, and maintainable solution that meets all requirements while keeping costs low through serverless services.\\\",\\n  \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\": \\\"delta-valerius-arch-01\\\"\\n}\\n###valerius-delta-arch-report-01###\"}],\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":3494,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":1292,\"service_tier\":\"standard\"}},\"latencyMs\":35598.60929200007}","genkit:state":"success"},"displayName":"anthropic/claude-4-opus","links":[],"instrumentationLibrary":{"name":"genkit-tracer","version":"v1"},"spanKind":"INTERNAL","sameProcessAsParentSpan":{"value":true},"status":{"code":0},"timeEvents":{"timeEvent":[]}},"91452531938d0c4f":{"spanId":"91452531938d0c4f","traceId":"f6f701